course: dictionary
lesson: 11979
title: The centilitre
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A centilitre is a small unit for measuring liquid, such as juice, milk or water. It is written cl. The word «centi-» means one hundredth, so a centilitre is one hundredth of a litre.
explain: A litre has 100 centilitres. A centilitre is also 10 millilitres. So you can change between them: to go from centilitres to millilitres, multiply by 10, and to go from millilitres to centilitres, divide by 10.
explain: Look for cl on drink bottles and cans. «The lemonade bottle holds 75 centilitres.» Because 75 is three-quarters of 100, that bottle holds three-quarters of a litre.
fact: A centilitre is written cl.
fact: 100 centilitres make 1 litre.
fact: 1 centilitre is 10 millilitres.
fact: «Centi-» means one hundredth, as in centimetre.
fact: The US spelling is centiliter.
exercise: «The cup holds 20 centilitres of water.» How many millilitres is that? | 2000 millilitres | 2 millilitres | 20 millilitres | *200 millilitres
exercise: What does the short form cl stand for? | kilolitre | *centilitre | centigram | centimetre
exercise: How many centilitres are in one litre? | 50 | 10 | *100 | 1000
test: Which is more: 75 centilitres or 1 litre? | 75 centilitres | *1 litre | They are the same
test: What does «centi-» mean in centilitre? | one hundred | one thousandth | *one hundredth | one tenth
exam: Sam pours 250 millilitres of water into a jug. How many centilitres is that? | 2.5 centilitres | 250 centilitres | 2500 centilitres | *25 centilitres
